LINT SIBLING ENFORCEMENT (the whole point of the layout-specific regex)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
[A] Inject `import { store } from "../state/store.ts";` into src/layout/layout.ts
    PASS→FAIL:  eslint FAILS with
      "19:1 error '../state/store.ts' import is restricted ... src/layout must
       not import from the state/ui layers  @typescript-eslint/no-restricted-imports"
    Restore →  eslint CLEAN.
[B] Inject `import type { Catalog } from "../data/types.ts";` (data is ALLOWED
    for layout, unlike the core block which bans it).
    Result:    eslint CLEAN (no import-ban error) — the layout regex
      `^\.\./(\.\./)*(state|ui)(/|$)` omits `data` by design.
    Restore →  eslint CLEAN.
=> The sibling block enforces state|ui bans while permitting data — proven both
   directions.


